48,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,26017,20590,57960,1975,1056,90,1808,31716,323,57960,1975,1056,90,11594,31716,315,57960,55114,19360,3,31796,518,400,39,12947,220,1416,57960,4044,425,1706,284,220,20,19,24884,43298,3,323,57960,4044,19360,284,220,20,17,24884,43298,54876,1221,1128,374,57960,4044,362,30725,3,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nAltitudes $\\overline{AD}$ and $\\overline{BE}$ of $\\triangle ABC$ intersect at $H$.  If $\\angle BAC = 54^\\circ$ and $\\angle ABC = 52^\\circ$, then what is $\\angle AHB$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"71c80aed10b21b16415166189e19eacea202f0b02d5a144e134e1de68253cc0b"},"seconds":6.679244041442871,"seed":11273910925730107,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\(\\angle AHB\\), we start by determining the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\). Since the sum of the angles in a triangle is \\(180^\\circ\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAC - \\angle ABC = 180^\\circ - 54^\\circ - 52^\\circ = 74^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the fact that the orthocenter \\(H\\) of a triangle is the point where the altitudes intersect. The key property we will use is that the measure of \\(\\angle AHB\\) is equal to \\(180^\\circ - \\angle ACB\\). This is because \\(\\angle AHB\\) is the angle formed by the intersection of the altitudes from \\(A\\) and \\(B\\), and it is supplementary to the angle \\(\\angle ACB\\) in the triangle.\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle AHB = 180^\\circ - \\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - 74^\\circ = 106^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(\\angle AHB\\) is \\(\\boxed{106^\\circ}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{106^\\circ}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:302"}
